Fix the single bug in /tmp/vcmp/w/t2/src/pricing.ts and nothing else.

Current applyDiscount:
```
/** pct is a whole percentage: applyDiscount(1000, 10) === 900. */
export function applyDiscount(cents: number, pct: number): number {
	return Math.round(cents * (1 - pct));
}
```

pct is a whole number (10 means 10%), but the body treats it as a fraction, so applyDiscount(1000, 10) returns a large negative number instead of 900.

Change only that return to:
```
	return Math.round(cents * (1 - pct / 100));
```

Leave subtotal, tax, the LineItem interface, and the doc comment unchanged. Do not edit tests or any other file. Do not run tests.

Fix the single bug in /tmp/vcmp/w/t2/src/inventory.ts and nothing else.

Current reserve:
```
/** Takes qty units if that many are left; returns whether it did. */
export function reserve(sku: string, qty: number): boolean {
	const have = stock.get(sku) ?? 0;
	if (have <= qty) { return false; }
	stock.set(sku, have - qty);
	return true;
}
```

The comparison uses <=, so reserving exactly the remaining units fails. Stock starts as A1=3, B2=0, C3=12. The intended behavior is: take qty units when have >= qty (including the last units) and return true; return false only when have < qty.

Change only that condition to:
```
	if (have < qty) { return false; }
```

Leave inStock, the stock map, and the doc comment unchanged. Do not edit tests or any other file. Do not run tests.

Fix the single bug in /tmp/vcmp/w/t2/src/checkout.ts and nothing else.

Current checkout:
```
/** Reserves every sku (throws 'out of stock <sku>' when one can't be), then returns the cart total. */
export function checkout(cart: Cart, skus: Array<[string, number]>, discountPct: number): number {
	for (const [sku, qty] of skus) {
		if (!reserve(sku, qty)) { continue; }
	}
	return cart.total(discountPct);
}
```

When reserve returns false the loop continues, so an out-of-stock sku is skipped instead of failing the checkout. The doc comment requires a throw of 'out of stock <sku>'.

Change only the continue to a throw:
```
		if (!reserve(sku, qty)) { throw new Error('out of stock ' + sku); }
```

Leave imports, the signature, and the doc comment unchanged. Do not edit tests or any other file. Do not run tests.

